--- /dev/null
+++ b/utils/podman/patches/021-overlay-lock-home-s-mount-for-the-lazy-feature-probes.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,138 @@
+From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] overlay: lock home's mount for the lazy feature probes
+
+The overlay driver probes some kernel features only when it is first
+asked about them: idmapped lower layers (SupportsShifting, so Status and
+the creation of a layer or a container), volatile mounts (Status, Get)
+and data-only lower layers. Each probe mounts in a new directory under
+home, then unmounts by path and removes the directory.
+
+The store holds its graph lock while it calls Init, which binds home
+onto itself unless it is a mount point already (mount.MakePrivate), and
+Cleanup, which unmounts it: the lock keeps these changes of home's mount
+apart from the mounts that Init's own probes make. The store does not
+hold it while it calls Status, or while it creates a layer or a
+container. When another process binds home meanwhile, the bind hides the
+probe's mounts: the probe's unmounts find no mount at their paths, the
+directory cannot be removed, and the mounts stay until a reboot, keeping
+the file system under the storage busy:
+
+  level=warning msg="Unmount \"/mnt/data/containers/storage/overlay/compat1721885628/lower-mapped\": invalid argument"
+
+It takes podman commands at once on a run root without the probes'
+records, as the first commands after a boot have.
+
+Hold a lock of the driver, in the run home, while Init binds home, while
+Cleanup unmounts it, and while a probe that runs after Init mounts under
+it.
+
+Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+---
+ .../storage/drivers/overlay/overlay.go        | 28 ++++++++++++++++++-
+ 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
